  "codebase_map": {
    "root_files": {
      "README.md": "Catalog of all eight agents with purpose, interface, capabilities, and run commands, plus Claude Code bash aliases (cld/cldp/uvr...). The map of the whole lesson.",
      "CLAUDE.md": "Essentially empty (single line) in this repo.",
      ".env.sample": "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, REPLICATE_API_TOKEN, GEMINI_API_KEY placeholders.",
      ".mcp.json.sample / .mcp.json.firecrawl_7k.sample / .mcp.json.playwright_10k.sample / .mcp.json.all_17k.sample": "MCP server configs sized by token cost (Firecrawl ~7k, Playwright ~10k, all ~17k) — the tokens each MCP server adds to context; rename off '.sample' to activate.",
      "ai_docs/README.md": "Pointers to the exact Anthropic docs the agents are built from — Claude Agent SDK (python/typescript), headless, MCP, sub-agents, slash-commands, hooks, custom-tools, and the SDK MIGRATION GUIDE (the claude_code_sdk -> claude_agent_sdk rename).",
      ".claude/": "The OUTER codebase's own agentic layer: command-based hooks (dangerous_command_blocker.py, universal_hook_logger.py), output styles, slash commands, TTS/LLM utils — distinct from the in-code SDK hooks inside the agents."
    },
    "agents": {
      "apps/custom_1_pong_agent/": "pong_agent.py (+ .ts), prompts/PONG_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md — system-prompt overwrite, query() one-off.",
      "apps/custom_2_echo_agent/": "echo_agent.py, prompts/ECHO_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md — @tool + in-memory MCP, Haiku, ClaudeSDKClient.",
      "apps/custom_3_calc_agent/": "calc_agent.py, prompts/CALC_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md — disallowed_tools, resume continuity, two tools.",
      "apps/custom_4_social_hype_agent/": "social_hype_agent.py + modules/{agent,tools,tts_notifier,utils}.py, prompts/SOCIAL_HYPE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md, social_hype_results.csv — WebSocket firehose stream agent.",
      "apps/custom_5_qa_agent/": "qa_agent.py, prompts/QA_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md, .claude/commands/qa_agent.md, .mcp.json.firecrawl_6k.sample, test_inline_hooks.py — hooks + Firecrawl MCP + parallel Task search.",
      "apps/custom_6_tri_copy_writer/": "backend/main.py (FastAPI), prompts/TRI_COPY_WRITER_SYSTEM_PROMPT.md, frontend/ (Vue) — agent as backend method, N variations, Pydantic response.",
      "apps/custom_7_micro_sdlc_agent/": "backend/main.py, backend/modules/{agent_orchestrator,config}.py, backend/db/database.py, backend/system_prompts/{PLANNER,REVIEWER}_*.md, backend/user_prompts/{PLANNER,BUILDER,REVIEWER}_*.md, frontend/ (Vue kanban), specs/ + reviews/ (generated plans/reviews) — three-agent SDLC with write-path hooks.",
      "apps/custom_8_ultra_stream_agent/": "backend/main.py, modules/data_types.py, system_prompts/{stream,inspector}_agent_system_prompt.md, generate_sample_data.py, data/ultra_stream_agent.jsonl, frontend/ (Vue dual-panel) — dual stream+inspector agents, chunked reads, self-managed context."
    },
    "generated_at_runtime": {
      "specs/*.md (agent 7)": "Plans written by the Planner agent (restricted to this dir).",
      "reviews/*.md (agent 7)": "Reviews written by the Reviewer agent (restricted to this dir).",
      "sdlc.db (agent 7) / ultra_stream.db (agent 8)": "SQLite stores for tickets / produced logs.",
      "social_hype_results.csv (agent 4)": "Appended analysis rows (timestamp, keywords, sentiment, summary, original text, raw data)."
    }
  },
  "current_practice_gaps": [
    {
      "gap": "The SDK was renamed from 'Claude Code SDK' to 'Claude Agent SDK'",
      "why": "Dan says 'Claude Code SDK' throughout and the on-screen code reads ClaudeCodeOptions, but the shipped repo already imports claude_agent_sdk and ClaudeAgentOptions in every file. The package renamed (claude_code_sdk -> claude-agent-sdk) circa late 2025; the migration guide is even linked in ai_docs. Read the recording's 'Claude Code SDK' as the Claude Agent SDK; install `claude-agent-sdk`.",
      "yt_candidates": [
        "6fCqj4xFCZI"
      ]
    },
    {
      "gap": "Course-era model IDs will be stale",
      "why": "Agents pin claude-sonnet-4-20250514, claude-3-5-haiku-20241022, and claude-opus-4-1-20250805. Current families are newer (e.g. Opus 4.x, Sonnet 5, Haiku 4.5, Fable 5) with different IDs. Dan future-proofs ('if you're operating in the future, hopefully you have something more powerful'). Swap the model strings; the model-selection principle (Haiku for trivial, Sonnet balanced, Opus for hard reasoning) is unchanged.",
      "yt_candidates": []
    },
    {
      "gap": "SDK message/block shapes may drift",
      "why": "The exact AssistantMessage/ResultMessage/*Block names and hook payload shape can change between SDK versions. Dan explicitly says 'these might change in the future — the key idea is that you understand how to manage the primitives.' Treat the parsing code as period-accurate; re-check against the current SDK reference before copying verbatim.",
      "yt_candidates": []
    },
    {
      "gap": "eval()-based math tool is a teaching simplification",
      "why": "The Calc agent evaluates expressions with eval() under a restricted __builtins__/math namespace. It's fine for the demo but modern practice prefers a real parser (ast.literal_eval or a math grammar) to avoid eval risk. Dan's own framing ('do whatever you want inside your tool, just return the proper format') invites hardening this in production.",
      "yt_candidates": []
    },
    {
      "gap": "Reusable-expertise-as-prompt-files vs first-class Agent Skills",
      "why": "These agents encode reusable expertise as system_prompts/*.md loaded by Python. Modern Claude Code also ships Agent Skills (SKILL.md with discovery/on-demand loading). Skills and SDK custom agents are complementary: Skills package expertise for the in-loop agent; the SDK is the right tool when you need PROGRAMMATIC control (custom tools, hooks, models, deployment) — which is this lesson's whole point.",
      "yt_candidates": [
        "X2ciJedw2vU"
      ]
    },
    {
      "gap": "QA agent MCP config path expects a rename",
      "why": "qa_agent.py loads .mcp.json.firecrawl_6k, but the file shipped on disk is .mcp.json.firecrawl_6k.sample. Out of the box the MCP config isn't found and the agent gracefully falls back to WebSearch/WebFetch. To use Firecrawl, drop the '.sample' suffix and set FIRECRAWL_API_KEY. A small but real setup gotcha for the lab.",
      "yt_candidates": []
    }
  ],
